  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.met.right": "Fee shown is correct",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.met.net": "Network calls (running total)",
  "track.sysdesign.cap.cache": "The screen on the left asks memory, then disk, then the server on the right; the tier that answers lights up.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s1.title": "0:00: open the screen, download 200 KB",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s1.explain": "Nothing is stored; every open is a full download.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.none.s1": "0:00: open the screen, download 200 KB",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s2.title": "0:02: open again, download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s2.explain": "The data has not changed, but the app cannot know, so it downloads everything.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.none.s2": "0:02: open again, download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s3.title": "0:10: open again, download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s3.explain": "Every open waits for the network; without signal the screen is empty.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.none.s3": "0:10: open again, download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s4.title": "0:30: the fee has changed; download 200 KB, show the correct 250,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.none.s4.explain": "Always right, but 800 KB downloaded for a list that barely changes.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.none.s4": "0:30: the fee has changed; download 200 KB, show the correct 250,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s1.title": "0:00: download 200 KB, store it on disk and in memory",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s1.explain": "The app stores it itself, ignoring every server header.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.forever.s1": "0:00: download 200 KB, store it on disk and in memory",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s2.title": "0:02: memory cache hit, shown at once",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s2.explain": "No network call. Fast.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.forever.s2": "0:02: memory cache hit, shown at once",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s3.title": "0:10: the process was killed; disk cache hit",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s3.explain": "The memory cache died with the process (chapter I2, \"Processes, memory and process death\"); the disk cache remains.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.forever.s3": "0:10: the process was killed; disk cache hit",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s4.title": "0:30: disk cache hit, shows the old 200,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.forever.s4.explain": "With no expiry, the app never asks again; the old fee stays until the app data is cleared.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.forever.s4": "0:30: disk cache hit, shows the old 200,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s1.title": "0:00: download 200 KB with Cache-Control: max-age=300",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s1.explain": "The server says: this copy is fresh for 300 seconds.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.maxage.s1": "0:00: download 200 KB with Cache-Control: max-age=300",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s2.title": "0:02: the copy is 2 minutes old, still fresh: reuse it",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s2.explain": "No network call within max-age.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.maxage.s2": "0:02: the copy is 2 minutes old, still fresh: reuse it",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s3.title": "0:10: the copy is 10 minutes old, stale: download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s3.explain": "The data has not actually changed, but without an ETag the app cannot ask cheaply.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.maxage.s3": "0:10: the copy is 10 minutes old, stale: download 200 KB again",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s4.title": "0:30: stale; download 200 KB, show the correct 250,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.maxage.s4.explain": "The fee is right. The price: for 5 minutes after a download, the app may show an old fee.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.maxage.s4": "0:30: stale; download 200 KB, show the correct 250,000",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s1.title": "0:00: download 200 KB with max-age=300 and ETag \"v7\"",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s1.explain": "The ETag is a version label for the content, chosen by the server.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.etag.s1": "0:00: download 200 KB with max-age=300 and ETag \"v7\"",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s2.title": "0:02: still fresh: reuse it",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s2.explain": "Same as max-age.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.etag.s2": "0:02: still fresh: reuse it",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s3.title": "0:10: stale; ask If-None-Match \"v7\", the server answers 304",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s3.explain": "If-None-Match is the header that asks \"is it still this version?\". 304 Not Modified has no content; the app updates the headers and reuses the stored copy. Just a few hundred bytes.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.etag.s3": "0:10: stale; ask If-None-Match \"v7\", the server answers 304",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s4.title": "0:30: ask If-None-Match \"v7\", the server answers 200 with \"v8\"",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.s.etag.s4.explain": "The content changed, so download the new 200 KB and show the correct 250,000. 401 KB in total instead of 800 KB.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.ev.etag.s4": "0:30: ask If-None-Match \"v7\", the server answers 200 with \"v8\"",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.try": "Walk all four steps of each approach; watch which tier answers and the fee shown at step 4.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.none.s2": "Alex Xu notes: consider caching when data is read often but changed rarely; a fee list is exactly that. [[src:book-xu1]]",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.none.s3": "With no stored copy, no network means no screen; offline-first (the app keeps working without a network) in the chapter \"Offline-first and background sync\" (H7) of the Saving Data on Android track solves it with a database.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.none.s4": "Right but costly: 4 × 200 KB for nearly the same list.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.forever.s2": "The memory cache is fastest, but lives only as long as the process.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.forever.s3": "A killed process loses its memory cache; see chapter I2, \"Processes, memory and process death\".",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.forever.s4": "Alex Xu advises: have an expiration policy; without one, data stays in the cache forever and can go stale. [[src:book-xu1]]",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.maxage.s2": "RFC 9111 (the standard for HTTP caching): a response (the server's reply) is fresh while its age has not exceeded its freshness lifetime; max-age gives that lifetime in seconds. [[src:rfc9111]]",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.maxage.s3": "RFC 9111: once stale, the cache must fetch or validate again; with no validator (a version label such as ETag, or Last-Modified: the last change time) only a full download remains. [[src:rfc9111]]",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.maxage.s4": "max-age is a promise of \"at most this stale\". Choose it by what the data can tolerate: a few minutes for fees, not for an account balance.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.etag.s2": "Within max-age, the ETag is not used yet.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.etag.s3": "RFC 9111: the cache sends the stored ETag in If-None-Match; a 304 means the stored response is updated and reused. RFC 9110: a 304 has no content. [[src:rfc9111]] [[src:rfc9110]]",
  "track.sysdesign.m.cache.co.etag.s4": "RFC 9111: a full response instead of a 304 means the stored copy is no longer suitable, and the cache uses the new one. [[src:rfc9111]]",
  "track.sysdesign.vz.tab.ca": "Cache tiers and headers",
  "track.sysdesign.vz.ca.cap": "The screen asks each tier top to bottom; the orange-outlined tier is the one that answers. A hit means the tier has a usable stored copy; a miss means it does not.",
